# Visual-authority source. authority-baseline.json hashes these files BYTE-FOR-BYTE,
# so git must not rewrite their line endings on checkout — a CRLF round-trip changes
# the bytes and therefore the aggregate, which would fail the certification gate on
# every fresh clone while the working tree still looked correct.
CrossBuy/Views/Inventory/*.cshtml               -text
CrossBuy/Views/Shared/_LayoutInventory.cshtml   -text
CrossBuy/wwwroot/Backend-assets/css/crossbuy-brand.css -text
CrossBuy/Views/Tasks/*.cshtml                   -text
CrossBuy/Views/Calendar/*.cshtml                -text

# Deployment manifests and package origins record exact SQL bytes. Preserve the
# qualified files on checkout; changing LF/CRLF would invalidate their evidence.
*.sql                                         -text
docs/roadmap-v2/*.md                           text eol=lf
docs/roadmap-v2/*.csv                          text eol=lf
governance/registry/*.json                     text eol=lf
